---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Shell from '../components/Shell.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import Byline from '../components/Byline.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/home/FinalCta.astro';
import quiz from '../data/exitReadiness.json';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { article, faqPage, advisors } from '../lib/schema';

const questions = quiz.questions;
const bands = quiz.bands;
const total = questions.length;
const updated = new Date(site.siteUpdated);
const reviewedBy = advisors.find((a) => a.founder) ?? advisors[0] ?? null;

const schema = [
  article({
    headline: 'Is my business ready to sell? A ten point readiness check',
    description:
      'Score your business against the ten things a buyer verifies before they price it. Instant result, no email required.',
    path: '/exit-readiness',
    published: updated,
    reviewedBy,
  }),
  faqPage(quiz.faq),
];

const crumbs = [{ href: '/exit-readiness', label: 'Exit readiness' }];

const opts = [
  { v: 'yes', label: 'Yes' },
  { v: 'partly', label: 'Partly' },
  { v: 'no', label: 'No' },
];
const chip =
  'block text-center text-sm rounded-2xl border border-black/10 dark:border-white/10 px-3 py-3 cursor-pointer transition-colors duration-500 ease peer-checked:border-accent peer-checked:bg-accent-soft peer-checked:text-accent-2 dark:peer-checked:bg-night-soft dark:peer-checked:text-[#7fd1b3] peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-accent';
---

<Base
  crumbs={crumbs}
  title="Is My Business Ready to Sell? Free 10 Point Check"
  description="Score your business against the ten things a buyer checks before pricing it: owner dependency, clean financials, lease, concentration. Instant result, no email needed."
  schema={schema}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Free tool"
    title="Is your business ready to sell?"
    intro="Ten questions, about three minutes, and a score out of 100. These are the things a buyer's accountant and lawyer actually test before they put a number on your business. No email required to see your result."
    crumbs={crumbs}
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
      <Button href="#check" variant="ink">Start the check</Button>
      <Button href="/valuation" variant="ring" icon="calculator">Get a valuation range</Button>
    </div>
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="max-w-wrap mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8 pb-16">
    <div class="prose-sbb reveal max-w-[68ch]">
      <p>
        Owners usually ask what their business is worth. The more useful question first is how much of that
        value a buyer can actually verify. A business earning S$1m that depends entirely on its owner, with
        two years of messy accounts and one customer at half of revenue, will not fetch what the profit
        suggests. The gap is not about the quality of what you built. It is about how much of it transfers.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each question below is something that comes up in due diligence on a real transaction. Answer
        honestly rather than optimistically: the point is to find the gaps before a buyer does, while you
        still have time and leverage to close them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="check" class="max-w-wrap mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8 pb-20 scroll-mt-28">
    <Shell radius="2rem" pad="2" shadow="frame">
      <form id="exitform" class="p-6 md:p-10" novalidate>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-ink-3 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] mb-4">
          <span>Answered</span>
          <span class="font-mono" data-q="count">0 / {total}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="h-1 bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/10 rounded-full mb-10 overflow-hidden">
          <div data-q="progress" class="h-1 bg-accent rounded-full transition-[width] duration-700 ease" style="width:0%"></div>
        </div>

        <ol class="space-y-10">
          {questions.map((q, i) => (
            <li>
              <fieldset data-name={q.id}>
                <legend class="font-medium text-base md:text-lg tracking-[-0.01em]">
                  <span class="font-mono text-accent dark:text-[#7fd1b3] text-sm mr-2">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                  {q.q}
                </legend>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-2 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light leading-relaxed max-w-[66ch]">{q.why}</p>
                <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 max-w-md">
                  {opts.map((o) => (
                    <div>
                      <input class="sr-only peer" type="radio" id={`${q.id}-${o.v}`} name={q.id} value={o.v} />
                      <label class={chip} for={`${q.id}-${o.v}`}>{o.label}</label>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </fieldset>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>

        <p data-q="incomplete" class="hidden mt-8 text-sm text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">
          Answer all {total} questions to see your score.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4">
          <Button type="button" id="exitsubmit" variant="accent" icon="arrow-right" class="js-only">Show my score</Button>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink-3 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light">
            Nothing is sent anywhere. The score is worked out in your browser.
          </p>
        </div>

        <noscript>
          <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-2 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light">
            Scoring needs JavaScript, but the checklist above works on its own. Count 10 for each yes and 5 for
            each partly. Below 45 out of 100, prepare before going to market. Above 75, you are close to ready.
            Or email <a class="underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will talk it through.
          </p>
        </noscript>
      </form>
    </Shell>

    <div data-q="result" class="hidden mt-6 scroll-mt-28 focus:outline-none">
      <Shell radius="2rem" pad="2" shadow="frame">
        <div class="p-6 md:p-10">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-3 dark:text-[#a9b4c2]">Your readiness score</p>
          <p class="mt-3 flex items-baseline gap-2">
            <span data-q="score" class="font-mono text-5xl md:text-6xl tracking-tight">0</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xl text-ink-3 dark:text-[#a9b4c2]">/ 100</span>
          </p>
          <p data-q="label" class="mt-4 text-2xl md:text-3xl font-medium tracking-[-0.02em]"></p>
          <p data-q="summary" class="mt-4 text-ink-2 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]"></p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-3 dark:text-[#a9b4c2]">What to do next</h2>
          <ul data-q="steps" class="mt-5 space-y-4 max-w-[62ch]"></ul>

          <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
            <Button href="/valuation" variant="accent" icon="calculator">Get an indicative range</Button>
            <Button href={site.bookingUrl} variant="ring" icon="envelope-simple">Email an advisor</Button>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-ink-3 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light max-w-[62ch]">
            This score is a preparation guide, not a valuation, and not financial advice. It weighs each of the
            ten factors equally, which is a simplification: in practice owner dependency and clean financials
            move the price further than the rest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Shell>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-wrap mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8 pb-20">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      {bands.map((b) => (
        <Shell radius="1.5rem" coreClass="p-6 h-full">
          <p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent dark:text-[#7fd1b3]">{b.min}+</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-medium">{b.label}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-2 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light leading-relaxed">{b.summary}</p>
        </Shell>
      ))}
    </div>
    <Byline published={updated} author={reviewedBy?.name} class="reveal mt-10" />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-wrap mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8 pb-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] reveal">Read next</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
      {[
        { href: '/guides/preparing-to-sell', t: 'Preparing your business for sale', d: 'The twelve month version of this checklist, in order of what moves the price most.' },
        { href: '/valuation', t: 'What is my business worth?', d: 'An indicative range from your sector, revenue and normalised profit, in about two minutes.' },
        { href: '/guides/valuation-methods', t: 'How SME valuation actually works', d: 'Why buyers price normalised EBITDA against a sector multiple, and what shifts the multiple.' },
        { href: '/sell-your-business', t: 'How the sale process runs', d: 'The five stages from mandate to completion, and how long each one really takes.' },
      ].map((l, i) => (
        <a href={l.href} class="reveal group rounded-[1.5rem] bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/[0.04] ring-1 ring-black/5 dark:ring-white/[0.08] p-1.5 transition-transform duration-700 ease hover:-translate-y-0.5" data-d={String((i % 2) + 1)}>
          <div class="rounded-[calc(1.5rem-0.375rem)] bg-white dark:bg-night-core p-6 h-full">
            <p class="font-medium group-hover:text-accent dark:group-hover:text-[#7fd1b3] transition-colors duration-500 ease">{l.t}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-2 dark:text-[#a9b4c2] font-light">{l.d}</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <Faq items={quiz.faq} heading="Questions about selling readiness" />

  <FinalCta />
</Base>

<script>
  import { initQuiz } from '../scripts/exitQuiz';
  import quiz from '../data/exitReadiness.json';
  const form = document.getElementById('exitform');
  if (form instanceof HTMLFormElement) initQuiz(form, quiz.bands, quiz.questions.length);
</script>
